WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.670
- This is Jeopardy!
♪♪♪

00:00:18.358 --> 00:00:21.200
- Tom, I'll start with you if that's OK.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.240
He's an NBA owner. A self-taught.
guitarist. And has guest-starred in

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.636
both "The Office" and "Game of Thrones."

00:00:29.636 --> 00:00:30.937
- Hmm.

00:00:30.937 --> 00:00:34.305
He's unhappy with his
boss and has no options.

00:00:34.305 --> 00:00:37.085
Who is Aaron Rogers?

00:00:37.085 --> 00:00:38.254
- Ding ding, that is correct.

00:00:38.254 --> 00:00:39.312
Well done.

00:00:39.312 --> 00:00:40.355
- That's a projection, Tom.

00:00:40.355 --> 00:00:42.081
I've never said I'm unhappy with my boss.

00:00:44.205 --> 00:00:47.885
- I said it, not you.
[Laughing]

00:00:47.885 --> 00:00:50.585
- Aaron, he taught himself
algebra at the age of six.

00:00:50.885 --> 00:00:57.525
He streams on Twitch under the
handle "TheBadOne23" and can sign his

00:00:57.525 --> 00:01:01.995
autograph backward with his left hand.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:04.137
- Phil, are you on Twitch?

00:01:04.137 --> 00:01:11.365
Yeah, I think that's
my teammate, uh, Bryson DeChambeau.

00:01:11.365 --> 00:01:12.865
- That would be correct.

00:01:12.865 --> 00:01:14.095
Well done.

00:01:14.095 --> 00:01:16.104
Bryson, this is one, this one's for you here.

00:01:16.104 --> 00:01:17.155
- Oh, boy.

00:01:17.155 --> 00:01:21.988
- He was a four-time All-America
selection, has the middle name

00:01:21.988 --> 00:01:26.985
"Alfred" and is right-handed.

00:01:26.985 --> 00:01:27.927
- Oh, my gosh.

00:01:27.927 --> 00:01:28.845
I got no idea.

00:01:28.845 --> 00:01:33.105
Um, I'm taking a complete guess on this.

00:01:33.105 --> 00:01:34.267
I don't know why.

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:36.645
No way it's my partner.

00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:38.095
Who is Aaron, who is Aaron Rodgers?

00:01:38.095 --> 00:01:39.205
I don't know.

00:01:39.205 --> 00:01:41.175
- It is "Who is Phil Mickelson?" actually.

00:01:41.175 --> 00:01:42.215
- No way.

00:01:42.215 --> 00:01:43.476
Did you know Phil is right-handed?

00:01:43.476 --> 00:01:46.446
- Phil, you never told me that, you son of a gun.

00:01:46.446 --> 00:01:49.445
- Bryson, I got, I got some news for you.

00:01:49.445 --> 00:01:53.850
I hate to tell you this. Phil doesn't like you.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:54.580
- I love Bryson.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.360
What are you talking about?

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.360
I love the guy.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:57.800
[Laughing]

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:58.458
- I didn't know that.

00:01:58.458 --> 00:01:59.840
See, I'd be terrible at Jeopardy.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.294
I'm more of a "Wheel of Fortune" guy.

00:02:01.294 --> 00:02:04.070
- Oh, sorry, Aaron.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.320
- No, that's not a knock on Aaron at all.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.790
- Teammate infighting already.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:08.539
I don't like it.

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:10.460
- OK. Gimme a break.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:13.345
- That's what we want: division from within.

00:02:13.345 --> 00:02:14.984
- I want to talk trash to somebody in this group.

00:02:14.984 --> 00:02:17.276
So if it has to be Bryson, so be it.

00:02:17.276 --> 00:02:18.125
[Laughing]

00:02:18.125 --> 00:02:19.115
- I've got one more question.

00:02:19.115 --> 00:02:20.246
This is for Phil.

00:02:20.246 --> 00:02:22.648
Phil, the answer to the question is,

00:02:22.648 --> 00:02:25.385
we're looking for the question, but the answer is: 

00:02:25.385 --> 00:02:27.053
"He led the New England Patriots

00:02:27.053 --> 00:02:29.225
to six Super Bowls, architect of one of the 

00:02:29.225 --> 00:02:33.515
greatest dynasties in the history of sports and is

00:02:33.515 --> 00:02:36.665
known far and wide as the GOAT."

00:02:36.665 --> 00:02:37.704
- Tom Brady is the GOAT.

00:02:37.704 --> 00:02:39.305
They also call him the man.

00:02:39.305 --> 00:02:41.167
Both seem to apply

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:45.945
and, uh, he's also my partner and I love it.

00:02:45.945 --> 00:02:47.407
- Most importantly. Your partner.

00:02:47.407 --> 00:02:49.584
- Can you form your answer in
the phrase of a question?

00:02:49.584 --> 00:02:50.094
- Honestly.

00:02:50.094 --> 00:02:53.179
- Question is: Who is the GOAT

00:02:53.179 --> 00:02:56.805
but also known as the man.

00:02:56.805 --> 00:02:58.545
And—

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.286
- Time's up.
[Beeper sounding]

00:03:00.286 --> 00:03:01.621
- Yeah, honestly.

00:03:01.621 --> 00:03:03.456
[Laughing]

00:03:03.456 --> 00:03:05.057
- [Imitating buzzer]

00:03:05.057 --> 00:03:07.560
[Laughing]

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.195
That wasn't double Jeopardy, we'd be broke.

00:03:09.195 --> 00:03:12.495
- Are you, are you saying: Who is Tom Brady?

00:03:12.495 --> 00:03:14.205
- I'm saying: Who is Tom Brady?

00:03:14.205 --> 00:03:15.375
- Ooh, no, Phil.

00:03:15.375 --> 00:03:15.885
I'm sorry.

00:03:15.885 --> 00:03:17.403
That would be Bill Belichick.

00:03:17.403 --> 00:03:20.673
[Laughing]

00:03:20.673 --> 00:03:21.135
I don't know.

00:03:21.135 --> 00:03:22.125
How'd that go, Aaron?

00:03:22.125 --> 00:03:24.277
I know you have, there's a little style

00:03:24.277 --> 00:03:25.755
when there's an incorrect answer.

00:03:25.755 --> 00:03:27.380
You don't want to shame the guy, but you

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.948
also want to make sure you get it right.

00:03:28.948 --> 00:03:31.275
- Aaron, he was amazing, by the way. 

00:03:31.275 --> 00:03:32.618
- He was.

00:03:32.618 --> 00:03:33.820
- A man of many talents.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.455
Just like, just like everything else he does.

00:03:35.455 --> 00:03:35.855
- I know.  

00:03:35.855 --> 00:03:37.123
- Phil, you probably didn't watch it.

00:03:37.123 --> 00:03:38.224
It's a little too intelligent for you,

00:03:38.224 --> 00:03:42.465
but, um, but thank you, Tom. ♪♪♪

